@appointment brennan-book
// SW2, 0.92.6 item 9 (the user: yes). A page in Brennan's book: after the lunch rush she asks you into the galley to taste
// three spoonfuls and tell her which is your favourite. It goes in her book of favourite dishes (canon), and it turns up
// on a Wednesday now and then (design-doc "Menus": a crew member's favourite on Wednesdays). The three spoons are dishes
// already on MENU.cycle; FX22 stores your pick as your favourite (the reply's mem word names it).
title: A page in Brennan's book
starts: invite
host: brennan
gate: tier>=acquaintance !mem:appt.brennan-book
when: weekday
at: 14:30-15:00
where: 3 room Galley: work:galley
who: host, you
once: yes
mem: appt.brennan-book
record: Your favourite dish is in Brennan's book.

== invite
- Got a minute after lunch tomorrow, love? Galley, half two. I need a taster.   #funny
- Half two tomorrow, come to the galley. Three spoons, one question. Don't eat lunch first.

== busy
- Not today, love, the cold store's sulking. Tomorrow, half two?

== mail
- Galley, {time} tomorrow. Brennan wants you to taste three things. Come hungry, she says, and honest.

== scene
brennan: Stool's there, love. Three spoons. Don't be polite. Tell me which.   [gesture]
brennan: First: my spiced lentils. Second: dumplings and greens. Third: the mushroom risotto. Go.
brennan: I keep a book. Every soul on this ship and the dish that makes them feel at home.   [nod]
brennan: Took me years to fill. Some of them took a month to tell me. You've got one spoon each.
? choice
* The lentils. Definitely the lentils.   flavour:share mem:appt.brennan-book.lentils
  brennan: Knew it. You went quiet on the first spoon. That's how I tell.   [laugh]
* The dumplings. I'd eat those every day.   flavour:cheer mem:appt.brennan-book.dumplings
  brennan: Every day? Wednesdays, love. I'm generous, not daft.   [laugh]
* The risotto. It tastes like somewhere I've been.   flavour:listen mem:appt.brennan-book.risotto
  brennan: That's the best reason there is. Don't tell me where. Not yet.   [nod]
brennan: There. Written in. In ink, so you can't change your mind. Now off you go, I've a dinner to make.   [gesture]

== thanks
- Brennan writes your favourite in her book, in ink, under your name. It'll turn up on a Wednesday one of these weeks.   #warm

== after
- Your dish is on Wednesday, love. Don't tell anyone it was you. Everyone will know.   #funny
- Saw your name in Brennan's book. Right next to the Captain's. Fancy.   #warm
